art they make brilliant tv shows really  but i said i'm too scared to sign up  without a script he joked to stern that  he does regret not getting the paycheck  when he realized how much tv stars  earned in the us  charlie sheen's departure from two and a  half men was quite the event making  headlines around the world and inspiring  a generation of quality memes and  hashtags in the years afterward though  many fans held on to a glimmer of hope  that he'd patch up his differences with  chuck lori and have one last rodeo on  the show as it turns out he nearly did  for the series finale the producers  reached out to him about a potential  appearance the plan was always to drop a  piano on charlie harper's head however  sheen wasn't interested in this  particular ending pitching his own  suggestion a scene that sets up a  spin-off sitcom called the harpers which  would have starred him and jon cryer  after the debacle that happened between  sheen and everyone else involved on two  and a half men let's just say that no  one jumped at his idea  so the episode went ahead with lori's  original ending and without a cameo from  sheen  while two and a half men focused on the  shenanigans caused by charlie and alan  harper the heart of the show was jake  who was played by angus t jones from his  pitch perfect comedic timing to his  undisputed chemistry with his  illustrious co-stars the nine-year-old  jones took all the acclimation right  from the get-go you get no allowance  that's your punishment for gambling told  you you'd do that  yeah you did  fans might expect that the casting for  the part of jake was a long arduous  process but it wasn't in fact chuck lori  told foundation interviews that jones  was the first and only child actor to  audition for the role the showrunner  added that he had seen jones performance  as hunter morris in 2002's the rookie  and invited him to read for the role of  jake after seeing how much fun jones was  having in the audition process and how  nonchalant he was about the whole thing  the decision to cast him was an easy one  it's no secret that the line where  charlie sheen ended and charlie harper  began was a blurred one at times many  fans didn't know if sheen was simply  playing a character or himself however  there was a particular moment off-screen  when the actor acted exactly like his tv  personality by lending a hand to john  cryer in his time of need in his  autobiography so that happened cryer  admitted that he was in a difficult  place after his divorce he decided to  hire a sex worker and sheen provided his  co-star with expert advice on the  industry pryor went on to explain  charlie suggested a few online purveyors  he occasionally used as this was when  prostitution was gaining a foothold on  the internet he and i had different  tastes so i didn't go with his exact  recommendations in another case of life  imitating art crier revealed that he  once brought a girlfriend to the set  only to be told by sheen that he'd dated  her in the past and that they'd broken  up because she wouldn't allow him to  bring another partner into the  relationship when ashton kutcher joined  two and a half men it surprised many  people including the actor himself  kutcher was a big movie star who was  proving himself a bankable name in the  industry so returning to the sitcom  world where he got his start seemed like  a backward move in an interview with  howard stern kutcher disclosed exactly  what swayed his decision to take the  role of walden schmidt his previous  agent worked for william morris  endeavour a company that was heavily  involved with two and a half men  at the time kutcher was considering  signing on the show was on track for  syndication if it was renewed for two  more seasons everyone involved could  expect a very nice payday kutcher  revealed that when he found out charlie  sheen was making 1.8 million dollars an  episode he told his agent he'd take the  job if he could get a similar deal  reportedly kutcher didn't get the same  offer as sheen but the rate he was  offered was clearly lucrative enough to  attach him to the sitcom for a full four  seasons i made a billion dollars doing  this billionaire entrepreneur walden  schmidt made his debut in season nine of  two and a half men where he buys charlie  harper's beach house and becomes allen's  new best friend and eventual husband  according to ashton kutcher though the  character of walden evolved quite a bit  in an interview on wtf with mark maron  kutcher explained that when he met with  chuck lorre to discuss the part of  walden lori pitched a character very  different from the walden that wound up  making it on screen  the actor never revealed the changes  made to the character between the pitch  and the first script but he did bring up  this observation to lorry the showrunner  told him walden's character arc was  going to take some time to unfold so  kutcher put faith in lori's vision and  went along for the ride  seeing how hit sitcoms such as will and  grace and matt about you have received  revivals in recent years many fans are  wondering if there's a chance that two  and a half men could get the same  treatment especially with the original  trio reprising their iconic roles while  charlie sheen has pushed for it with the  harper's concept jon cryer isn't exactly  rushing back to the malibu beach house  anytime soon when asked about his  current relationship with sheen on  access crier stated it's kind of a  roller coaster when you have charlie in  your life and i just haven't decided to  get back on that roller coaster maybe he  needs a few extra zeros on a new  contract to help twist his arm  there were several supporting characters  on two and a half men but none of them  had the charisma or hilarity of berta  the housekeeper whether she was pointing  out the obvious or sticking around to  laugh at the harper fallouts the  outspoken berta never missed a beat  however the character could have been  very different if it wasn't for the late  conchata farrell's desire to do things  her own way in an interview with the av  club farrell explained that the  showrunners had asked her to adopt an  eastern european accent when playing the  character when she went in for the  audition she told the room that despite  the fact that she can do a pretty solid  russian accent she thought that adopting  a quote trailer park dialect was a  better fit for the character next thing  i know i'm bellying up on the floor  hacking out along while the cops are  dragging out bonnie and claude in  handcuffs farrell's performance  impressed chuck lorre and everyone else  who decided to go along with her  suggestion in fact they loved it so much  that they extended her presence on the  show far beyond the initially planned  two episode arc while the spotlight was  firmly on charlie sheen during his  ongoing feud with chuck lorre hardly  anyone ever considered what the  showrunner went through as their  conflict unfolded entertainment weekly  reports that laurie was deeply hurt by  the ordeal so much so that he  contemplated leaving two and a half men  in 2011. laurie recounted a conversation  he had with other showrunners to tv  guide i offered to quit the show last  winter i said listen if for some reason  i'm now the antichrist i'm happy to  leave it's not in my interest to stop  the show and i certainly don't want to  put all these people out of work keep  going get another guy don't stop on my  account however cbs had lori's back and  he described the network's decision to  fire sheen as a choice based on ethics  rather than money personal and  professional disagreements are common in  any industry including television  sometimes one party just might not be  feeling a script or the direction in  which the series is going they can even  part ways because of creative  differences but still remain friends  unfortunately charlie sheen didn't get  that memo not only did he burn his  bridges with chuck lori but he also  painted the town red with metaphorical  tiger blood while it appeared that sheen  would never squash his feud with lori  time does heal all wounds in an  interview with the guardian sheen was  asked about his regrets the first thing  he said was that he should have handled  leaving two and a half men more  thoughtfully  he also admitted to people that there  were numerous approaches he could have  taken to handle the conflict and that  he's unhappy with the one he chose  is it possible that by sheen admitting  his wrong he and laurie could work  together again in the future anything is  possible in hollywood  charlie sheen's departure from two and a  half men could have played out like a  scene from the show bad vibes and verbal  jabs were thrown around in the press  like a game of hot potato one of the  people who caught some collateral damage  in the process was ashton kutcher for  all intents and purposes he'd done  nothing wrong by accepting the role of  walden schmidt in the sitcom however  that didn't stop sheen from taking to  twitter and insulting kutcher on several  occasions  kutcher didn't take the attacks lying  down though and fired back when required  after a while sheen's comments stopped  bothering him completely charlie's seen  his become like a  parent on charlie brown to me it's more  like wah  years later sheen apologized and  admitted that he shouldn't have behaved  the way he did towards kutcher sheen  told the kyle and jackie o radio show i  was stupidly mean to him because i  overlooked the reality and difficulty of  taking over a show he also expressed  empathy for kutcher explaining that he  had done the same thing by taking over  from michael j fox on spin city luckily  sheen and kutcher appear to have put  their beef behind them when kutcher ran  into sheen at a baseball game the pair  even shook hands  out of all the characters in two and a  half men the most memeable was alan  harper from him constantly forgetting  his wallet to refusing to move out of  his brother's malibu beach house allen  was the ultimate sponge however chuck  lorre's initial vision for the character  of alan was very different from the one  that appeared on screen in fact he and  the show's co-creator lee aronson plant  something of biblical proportions in a  conversation with the hollywood reporter  laurie said alan was always designed  from the get-go to be kind of the  biblical job the good man who is trying  his best and can't catch a break and the  character has morphed over the gears and  become much broader the showrunner  admitted that while that was the plan  the character deviated from it as the  series found its feet charlie on the  other hand was supposed to be symbolic  of dionysus the god of wine and  fertility that one seems to have stuck  throughout  charlie harper had many lovers on two  and a half men but there were a select  few who almost tamed the wild man  one of these individuals was jennifer  taylor's character chelsea the actress  had appeared on the show in smaller  parts before being cast as chelsea in  season six  what many fans don't realize is how the  sitcom gave taylor the exact  professional and financial boost she  needed at the time while chatting with  entertainment journalist jeremy roberts  taylor opened up about how she had just  given birth to her daughter and was  preparing to sell her house to make ends  meet when she got the part she  considered the timing a good omen and  began filming for the recurring role in  2008  [Music]

